    "updated_at": "2026-01-13T02:21:41Z",
    "body": "When trying to reproduce, I noticed that qwen2.5-coder:14b sometimes fails call tools correctly, producing the output shown in the screenshot.\n\n<img width=\"1112\" height=\"790\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/683cf3ec-df1e-48d4-8f61-aad289367fa5\" />\n\nAfter debugging, I believe the issue lies with the model itself rather than Continue. I've also seen lots of discussion on the wrong tool calling problem with this model. Here are some of them:\n[https://github.com/QwenLM/Qwen3-Coder/issues/180](url)\n[https://www.reddit.com/r/LocalLLaMA/comments/1j30cnp/qwen25_32b_sometimes_will_put_tool_calls_in_the/](url)\n\nInterestingly, such wrong tool calling still can be applied in Continue, resulting the same issue @chavdarb  described where all the file content is replace by thinking message.\n\nMaybe the easiest solution to this issue is, just change to another model, or, I can write a tool call parser for this specific model. If this makes sense to the maintainer @RomneyDa , I'd be happy to take this issue. If not, I'd love to hear your thoughts. Should we leave it as a known limitation for now, or is there another direction you'd prefer?",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
